!    Reactants                    Products                                                  A          B          C          D        F         ITYPE Tmin   Tmax formula ID xxxxx
! formula: 1 = Cosmic-ray ionization, 2 = Photo-dissociation (Draine), 3 = Modified Arrhenius, 4 = ionpol1, 5 = ionpol2 
! Critical reactions:
! k(S+O2) = 4e-12 (Fuente et al 2017 propose 4.8e-12, calcul d'Octavio/Varandas)
! k(O+OH) = 1e-11 to increase OH, NO and SO2 (rate comprised between 2e-11 and 4e-11 with log_uniform distribution).
! k(O+CN) = 1.5e-10 (preliminary experiment with Kevin)
! k(C+HNC) = 5e-11 to take into account the back dissociation of HNCC
! N+ + H2 pour o-H2/p-H2 = 1 (Flower 2006). Voir fichier N(+)+H2.R dans N(+)+H2
! O + c-C3H2 -> HC3O + H may be very low but is hardly strictly zero 
! small rate for C3H3+ + H2 and C3H5+ + H2 to allow CH3CCH and C3H6 formation
! small branching ratio for C3H5+ + e- -> C3H3 + H + H and C3H7+ + e- -> C3H5 + H + H to minimize C3H3 + O, C3H5 + O
! small branching ratio for C3H7+ + e- -> CH3 + C2H4 to avoid to produce potentially articficially C2H4 when C3H3+ and C3H5+ can react with H2
